85
00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.283
No, it's true!

86
00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:43.726
I did, I did, I did.

87
00:02:43.726 --> 00:02:46.714
You probably, when you go like,

88
00:02:46.714 --> 00:02:48.536
"When was the first I had sex?"

89
00:02:48.536 --> 00:02:50.574
You have to remember, you go through this memory.

90
00:02:50.574 --> 00:02:53.407
I can just rent a film, basically.

91
00:02:54.598 --> 00:02:56.072
You know exactly when it happened?

92
00:02:56.072 --> 00:02:57.478
Yes, I know exactly.

93
00:02:57.478 --> 00:03:00.153
It was this amazing actress, beautiful,

94
00:03:00.153 --> 00:03:03.974
and I was dreaming about it, and I felt the luckiest.

95
00:03:03.974 --> 00:03:04.990
I was 12 years old.

96
00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:05.823
12?

97
00:03:05.823 --> 00:03:06.656
Yeah.

98
00:03:06.656 --> 00:03:07.875
You had a sex scene when you were 12?

99
00:03:07.875 --> 00:03:08.831
Oh, yeah.

100
00:03:08.831 --> 00:03:10.166
(audience laughing)

101
00:03:10.166 --> 00:03:12.048
But I arrived, and I was very nervous,

102
00:03:12.048 --> 00:03:14.925
and I was just like, "Well, I hope she likes it then,

103
00:03:14.925 --> 00:03:16.090
and after the scene,

104
00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.418
because I know it's not gonna be sex,

105
00:03:17.418 --> 00:03:19.479
but then something can start from there," right?

106
00:03:19.479 --> 00:03:20.312
Yeah.

107
00:03:20.312 --> 00:03:21.888
And then I get there,

108
00:03:21.888 --> 00:03:24.797
and there I see 40 people looking at me with the camera.

109
00:03:24.797 --> 00:03:25.984
They got the cameras, yeah, everything.

110
00:03:25.984 --> 00:03:27.303
And I go like, "Shit!"

111
00:03:27.303 --> 00:03:28.868
And I can just think of like,

112
00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:29.954
"Ah, I don't wanna have a hard,

113
00:03:29.954 --> 00:03:32.948
please, please, please, I don't wanna get too excited,"

114
00:03:32.948 --> 00:03:34.089
you know, that kind of thing.

115
00:03:34.089 --> 00:03:34.922
Yeah, yeah.

116
00:03:34.922 --> 00:03:36.422
And obviously it didn't happen.

117
00:03:36.422 --> 00:03:38.170
I was 12; I couldn't control it.

118
00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.566
She was very nice.

119
00:03:39.566 --> 00:03:40.733
She'd hide it.

120
00:03:41.792 --> 00:03:43.089
She took good care of you, that's the important thing.

121
00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:43.922
She took good care,

122
00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:45.750
but I started doing telenovelas, you know, here.

123
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.975
Yeah, you started doing telenovelas.

124
00:03:46.975 --> 00:03:48.844
It was your training, and then, of course,

125
00:03:48.844 --> 00:03:49.677
what's happened to you

126
00:03:49.677 --> 00:03:51.445
since then has been absolutely spectacular.

127
00:03:51.445 --> 00:03:52.278
It has.

128
00:03:52.278 --> 00:03:53.661
Rogue One: A Star Wars Story.

129
00:03:53.661 --> 00:03:57.583
Significant. I mean, biggest film in the world,

130
00:03:57.583 --> 00:04:01.965
and such a big deal for a Latino to be a lead

131
00:04:01.965 --> 00:04:03.483
in a Star Wars movie.

132
00:04:03.483 --> 00:04:05.510
This was a seismic change.

133
00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.814
It meant a lot, and it meant a lot for,

134
00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:10.679
I mean, today, in this time, this happening.

135
00:04:10.679 --> 00:04:12.609
It's not a coincidence.

136
00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:15.882
I read many things, and there was a beautiful thing

137
00:04:15.882 --> 00:04:18.549
that a girl from San Diego wrote

138
00:04:19.554 --> 00:04:23.337
about the experience of having her father watching the film,

139
00:04:23.337 --> 00:04:27.098
and how the father reacted to my character and the accent,

140
00:04:27.098 --> 00:04:29.225
and feeling represented on the screen.

141
00:04:29.225 --> 00:04:30.641
So the father, of course, was Mexican?

142
00:04:30.641 --> 00:04:32.341
The father was an immigrant, yeah.

143
00:04:32.341 --> 00:04:34.942
An immigrant, and he saw, and he couldn't believe--

144
00:04:34.942 --> 00:04:35.775
He couldn't believe it.

145
00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.558
He was watching a Star Wars film,

146
00:04:37.558 --> 00:04:39.400
and that his accent was represented,

147
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.476
that he knew who I was.

148
00:04:41.476 --> 00:04:42.367
That's amazing.

149
00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:43.696
(audience applauding)

150
00:04:43.696 --> 00:04:46.921
Yeah, I mean, I think it's the kind

151
00:04:46.921 --> 00:04:49.365
of medicine we're talking about in these times.

152
00:04:49.365 --> 00:04:50.393
We need that medicine.

153
00:04:50.393 --> 00:04:52.135
We need that medicine.

154
00:04:52.135 --> 00:04:55.176
I have, obviously we're doing a lot of comedy here,

155
00:04:55.176 --> 00:04:58.253
but on a personal level, I've talked to many,

156
00:04:58.253 --> 00:05:00.517
many Mexicans since I arrived,

157
00:05:00.517 --> 00:05:03.470
and this is the biggest feeling that I get from them.

158
00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.589
They feel misunderstood, and their feelings are hurt

159
00:05:06.589 --> 00:05:08.795
on a very simple, human level.

160
00:05:08.795 --> 00:05:11.499
Specific politics aside, they've heard these things

161
00:05:11.499 --> 00:05:13.611
that were said at campaign rallies,

162
00:05:13.611 --> 00:05:15.775
they've heard this chant, "Build the wall,"

163
00:05:15.775 --> 00:05:17.819
they've heard certain words used about them,

164
00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:19.918
and I've spent a lot of time trying to explain to them

165
00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:23.135
many people in the United States love the Mexican people.

166
00:05:23.135 --> 00:05:25.019
This is a misrepresentation of how people feel.

167
00:05:25.019 --> 00:05:26.105
Definitely.

168
00:05:26.105 --> 00:05:27.886
And I think that needs to come across.

169
00:05:27.886 --> 00:05:31.698
(audience applauding)

170
00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:34.430
I agree, and I think those people

171
00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.836
that are afraid of being deported today,

172
00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.316
their voice has been silent,

173
00:05:39.316 --> 00:05:41.519
and we have to make sure their stories are told

174
00:05:41.519 --> 00:05:42.894
in and out of States,

175
00:05:42.894 --> 00:05:45.818
and that they get their stories matter to us,

176
00:05:45.818 --> 00:05:48.130
because they need that strength to keep going,

177
00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:51.863
and ignorance, we can fight with love and with understanding

178
00:05:51.863 --> 00:05:55.154
and with things like what you are doing, showing respect.

179
00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.479
We've wanted this to be a very positive experience,

180
00:05:58.479 --> 00:06:01.247
and what's the most beautiful thing for me is that--

181
00:06:01.247 --> 00:06:04.462
You wanted sex, I mean, don't get us confused.

182
00:06:04.462 --> 00:06:06.714
I mean, you came, and you ask a producer,

183
00:06:06.714 --> 00:06:08.575
"Please, I want to have sex."

184
00:06:08.575 --> 00:06:10.694
Listen, please. Okay, yes, okay.

185
00:06:10.694 --> 00:06:11.527
That was clear.

186
00:06:11.527 --> 00:06:14.271
Okay. Numero uno: sex, okay?

187
00:06:14.271 --> 00:06:17.192
But numero dos was to bring positivity--

188
00:06:17.192 --> 00:06:19.503
(Conan, Diego, and audience laughing)

189
00:06:19.503 --> 00:06:21.586
Come on! Give me a break.

190
00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:26.583
To the people of Mexico, and let them know

191
00:06:27.471 --> 00:06:30.701
that we hear them, that they are heard,

192
00:06:30.701 --> 00:06:33.371
and that what is so nice is that so many of them,

193
00:06:33.371 --> 00:06:34.924
when they've had an opportunity to speak,

194
00:06:34.924 --> 00:06:36.777
I don't get a lot of anger from them,

195
00:06:36.777 --> 00:06:39.363
I get them talking in a very beautiful, eloquent way,

196
00:06:39.363 --> 00:06:42.060
saying, "We need to come together. We're really--

197
00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.073
It's about empathy, yeah.

198
00:06:43.073 --> 00:06:46.987
It's empathy. Which makes me feel happy.

199
00:06:46.987 --> 00:06:51.154
Well, I say we end on a positive note, which is we drink.

200
00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.233
I am an optimist, and I think better times are coming,

201
00:06:56.233 --> 00:06:57.521
so Viva Mexico!

202
00:06:57.521 --> 00:06:58.354
Viva Mexico! Salud!

203
00:06:58.354 --> 00:07:01.671
(audience applauding)

204
00:07:01.671 --> 00:07:03.867
Rogue One: A Star Wars Story will be available

205
00:07:03.867 --> 00:07:07.990
